---
import:
  - stdlib/lang/python
  - stdlib/cli/common
description: A command-line tool in Python 3.12 with Click 8.
---

***implementation reqs***

- :Implementation: uses Click 8, in the package `app/`.
  - `app/cli.py` holds the `@click.group()` with `--verbose`, `--debug` and `--version`, which sets up logging, and one module per command in `app/commands/`.
  - The work lives in `app/core/`, and the tool's errors in `app/errors.py`, under one base class `ToolError`, a subclass of `click.ClickException` whose `exit_code` is 1.
  - `[project.scripts]` names the tool, `<tool> = "app.cli:cli"`.
- :Implementation: sets up the standard `logging` module to write to standard error with the level `--verbose` or `--debug` gives.
- :UnitTests: run commands with Click's `CliRunner`.
